  "decision": "replace_ranges",
  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained shift starting around index 574 (N drops ~13, E rises ~17, U drops ~20) and persisting through index 630, then a return-like step at index 631 (N jumps +15, E drops -15, U jumps +20), consistent with a temporary platform. P1 and P2 are isolated single-day candidates unsupported by interior observations; P3 (577–631) captures the bulk of the offset but ends *at* the return, not before it; P4 and P5 are the return steps. The only genuine temporary platform is the interval from onset (~574) to just *before* the return (~630), i.e., indices 574–630. However, no candidate pair covers this cleanly: P3 starts too late (577) and includes the return day (631); P1/P2 are spurious spikes. Since no supplied pair correctly isolates the temporary platform without including the return or missing onset, and evidence supports a single temporary offset from ~574 to ~630, we replace ranges with an empty set—no supplied pair is a genuine platform per strict criteria (sustained shift + opposing return on same axes, interior consistency).",
  "pair_ids": []
}
